{"created": "2024-05-27T11:55:50.183216+00:00", "modified": "2024-05-27T11:55:50.972313+00:00", "id": 10852695, "conceptrecid": "10852694", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10852695", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10852694", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10852695", "metadata": {"title": "Probability dsitributed equivalent circuit model - Matlab code", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10852695", "publication_date": "2024-03-22", "description": "<h2>General information</h2>\n<p>The code stored in this repository can be used to reproduce the results described in the publication \"A physically motivated hysteresis model for lithium-ion batteries using a probability distributed equivalent circuit\" published in Nature Communications Engineering in 2024 by Jahn et al.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Written in Matlab 2020b, download data folder with parameter sets and measurement data from:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10852930\">www.doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10852930</a></p>\n<p>Store the data in a folder named \"Data\" at the same location as the Matlab scripts to run all scripts without changes to the code.</p>\n<h2>Code description</h2>\n<h3>pdecm_lr_solver.m</h3>\n<p>Solves the equivalent circuit model (ECM) consisting out the probability distributed ECM and an optional preconnected R-2RC model in state space representation with the LR factorization. Input and outputs are documented in the code header.</p>\n<h3>pdecm_fullcell.m</h3>\n<p>Uses pdecm_lr_solver.m to simulate a graphite and a LFP half-cell with optimized parameter sets. These parameter were optimized by comparing simulation and measurement results of half-cells. The measurement data can be found under the Zenodo repository linked above. The output of the function is the full-cell simulation given by the difference of both half-cells at every time step.&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>hys_sim_referenceCase.m</h3>\n<p>Code to simulate the influences of the parameter of the probability distributed ECM on different defined test cases using a hypothetical non-monotonous single particle open circuit potential curve. Sets up all inputs and plots the results of the calculations done by pdecm_lr_solver.m.</p>\n<h3>hys_lfp_fc_sim.m</h3>\n<p>Defines different test scenarios for the simulation of a commercial graphite|LFP cell and plots the results as well as deviation from measurements. The measurement data can be found under the Zenodo repository linked above. The script executes pdecm_fullcell.m to get the resulting voltage response of the full-cell.</p>\n<h3>hys_plett_sim.m</h3>\n<p>Matlab code using a simple single-state hysteresis model as established by Gregory Plett to simulate the voltage response of a commercial graphite|LFP cell.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jahn, Leonard", "affiliation": "University of Bayreuth", "orcid": "0000-0001-6496-4747"}, {"name": "Moessle, Patrick", "affiliation": "University of Bayreuth", "orcid": "0000-0001-5496-8437"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Danzer, Michael A.", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e4t Bayreuth", "type": "ContactPerson", "orcid": "0000-0002-4135-7263"}, {"name": "R\u00f6der, Fridolin", "affiliation": null, "type": "ContactPerson", "orcid": "0000-0002-1547-3885"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.10852930", "relation": "requires", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1038/s44172-024-00221-4", "relation": "isPublishedIn", "resource_type": "publication", "scheme": "doi"}], "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "matlab", "title": {"en": "MATLAB"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software documentation", "type": "publication", "subtype": "softwaredocumentation"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "03XP0321A", "internal_id": "04pz7b180::03XP0321A", "funder": {"name": "Federal Ministry of Education and Research"}, "title": "BMBF Project HysKaDi", "url": "https://www.aqua-cluster.de/de/projekte/hyskadi/"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "10852694"}}]}}, "title": "Probability dsitributed equivalent circuit model - Matlab code", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10852695", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10852695?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10852695", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10852695", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10852695", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852694", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10852694", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10852694", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10852694", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10852695/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10852695/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10852695/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10852695/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/108